  "articleBody": "Designing a basement remodel without catching hidden constraints early leads to expensive redesigns during construction. Here are the most frequent planning errors to watch for:\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n1. Covering damp foundation walls without mitigation. Trapping groundwater behind insulation ruins drywall and framing. Moisture issues must be corrected at the perimeter first.\n2. Forgetting mechanical access requirements. Enclosing a furnace or water heater too tightly violates service clearances and makes maintenance impossible.\n3. Overlooking egress window placement. You cannot designate a room as a legal bedroom without meeting specific emergency escape window requirements.\n4. Designing without verifying structural posts. Trying to create an open concept layout by removing or shifting posts without an engineer's review creates safety risks.\n5. Inaccurate ceiling height calculations. Ductwork and plumbing lines drop down below joists, altering real finished headroom.\n\nWhen structural alterations or below-grade moisture controls are needed, experienced professional guidance keeps your plans compliant. HH Remodeling LLC works with Denver area homeowners to design practical, well-planned basements. Call 303-505-0866 to talk through your basement design ideas.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
